---
import BaseLayout from "../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import Header from "../../components/Header.astro";
import Footer from "../../components/Footer.astro";
import HairPhaseIllustration from "../../components/HairPhaseIllustration.astro";
import { growthPhases } from "../../data/brand";

const structuredData = {
  "@context": "https://schema.org",
  "@type": "Article",
  headline: "The four stages of the hair-growth cycle",
  datePublished: "2026-09-14",
  dateModified: "2026-09-14",
  inLanguage: "en-GB",
  author: { "@type": "Organization", name: "CYPH/1" },
  publisher: { "@type": "Organization", name: "CYPH/1" }
};
---
<BaseLayout
  title="The four stages of the hair-growth cycle | CYPH/1"
  description="Understand anagen, catagen, telogen and exogen, and why the hair-growth cycle matters in IPL."
  structuredData={structuredData}
>
  <Header />
  <main id="main" class="article-page">
    <article>
      <header class="article-hero section">
        <div class="container article-reading">
          <p class="eyebrow">Know the cycle · Hair-growth science</p>
          <h1 data-reveal>The four stages of the hair-growth cycle</h1>
          <p class="lede">Hair does not grow continuously or all at once. Individual follicles move through a repeating cycle commonly described as anagen, catagen, telogen and exogen.</p>
          <p class="article-meta">Published 14 September 2026 · General educational content</p>
        </div>
      </header>

      <section class="section article-section" aria-labelledby="cycle-overview">
        <div class="container article-reading">
          <p class="section-index">01 / The cycle</p>
          <h2 id="cycle-overview" data-reveal>Four phases, different roles.</h2>
          <p>At any one time, different hairs can be at different points in their cycle. Understanding those phases provides useful context for why light-based hair reduction is approached as a repeated routine rather than a one-off event.</p>
        </div>
        <ol class="container article-phase-grid">
          {growthPhases.map((phase) => (
            <li class:list={{ active: phase.active }} data-phase-card>
              <div class="phase-card-meta"><span>{phase.number}</span>{phase.active && <small>Phase one</small>}</div>
              <HairPhaseIllustration phase={phase.name} />
              <h3>{phase.name}</h3>
              <p class="phase-label">{phase.label}</p>
              <p class="phase-description">{phase.description}</p>
              {phase.name === "Anagen" && <p class="phase-motion-note">Illustrative light pulse · general IPL principle</p>}
            </li>
          ))}
        </ol>
      </section>

      <section class="section article-section">
        <div class="container article-reading article-copy">
          <p class="section-index">02 / Phase by phase</p>
          <h2 data-reveal>Anagen — active growth</h2>
          <p>Anagen is the active-growth phase. During this stage, the follicle produces the hair shaft. Light-based hair reduction is associated with active growth, which is one reason treatment is repeated across the hair cycle.</p>
          <h2 data-reveal>Catagen — transition</h2>
          <p>Catagen is a short transition, or regression, phase in which active growth stops.</p>
          <h2 data-reveal>Telogen — rest</h2>
          <p>Telogen is a resting phase in which the existing hair is no longer actively growing.</p>
          <h2 data-reveal>Exogen — shedding</h2>
          <p>Exogen describes the release and shedding of the existing hair. Some scientific sources treat exogen as part of telogen rather than a completely separate phase, which is why CYPH/1 describes the four-stage model as one that is commonly used.</p>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section class="section article-section">
        <div class="container article-reading article-copy">
          <p class="section-index">03 / Why it matters for IPL</p>
          <h2 data-reveal>A repeated routine, not phase detection.</h2>
          <p>IPL treatment does not identify the growth phase of an individual hair. Different hairs can be at different points in the cycle, so light-based hair reduction is repeated over time to allow treatment to coincide with hairs entering active growth.</p>
          <aside class="science-note">
            <p><strong>Important distinction.</strong> “Target the growth” describes the CYPH/1 brand principle. It does not mean that a future CYPH/1 device can detect the growth phase of an individual hair.</p>
          </aside>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section class="section article-section" aria-labelledby="sources">
        <div class="container article-reading article-copy">
          <p class="section-index">04 / Sources</p>
          <h2 id="sources" data-reveal>Evidence behind this article.</h2>
          <p>This article is general hair-cycle and IPL education. It does not make performance, safety or suitability claims about a future CYPH/1 product.</p>
          <ul class="article-sources">
            <li><a href="https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/books/NBK470321/">NCBI Bookshelf — Anatomy, Hair Follicle</a></li>
            <li><a href="https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC9917549/">International Journal of Molecular Sciences — Hair Growth Cycle and Hair Loss</a></li>
            <li><a href="https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC5475414/">Journal of Cutaneous and Aesthetic Surgery — Photoepilation and Skin Photorejuvenation</a></li>
            <li><a href="https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC4745852/">Clinical, Cosmetic and Investigational Dermatology — Lasers and Intense Pulsed Light Technology</a></li>
          </ul>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section class="section article-cta">
        <div class="container article-reading">
          <p class="eyebrow">Cycle. Phase. One.</p>
          <h2 data-reveal>Follow the CYPH/1 journey.</h2>
          <p>Join early access for product-development updates and launch information. Registration is not an order or pre-order.</p>
          <a class="button" href="/">Explore CYPH/1</a>
        </div>
      </section>
    </article>
  </main>
  <Footer />
</BaseLayout>

<script>
  const reduceMotion = window.matchMedia("(prefers-reduced-motion: reduce)").matches;
  const revealTargets = document.querySelectorAll("[data-reveal], [data-phase-card]");

  if (reduceMotion || !("IntersectionObserver" in window)) {
    revealTargets.forEach((target) => target.classList.add("is-visible"));
  } else {
    const observer = new IntersectionObserver((entries) => {
      entries.forEach((entry) => {
        if (!entry.isIntersecting) return;
        entry.target.classList.add("is-visible");
        observer.unobserve(entry.target);
      });
    }, { threshold: 0.18, rootMargin: "0px 0px -8% 0px" });

    revealTargets.forEach((target) => observer.observe(target));
  }
</script>

<style>
  .article-reading { max-width: var(--cyph-layout-reading); }
  .article-hero { padding-bottom: var(--cyph-layout-section-compact); }
  .article-hero h1 {
    max-width: 13ch;
    margin: var(--cyph-space-4) 0 var(--cyph-space-6);
    font-size: clamp(2.4rem, 5.7vw, 4.9rem);
    line-height: 1.08;
  }
  .article-meta { margin-top: var(--cyph-space-6); color: var(--cyph-text-secondary); font-size: .875rem; }
  .article-section { padding-block: var(--cyph-layout-section-compact); }
  .article-page h2 {
    max-width: 22ch;
    font-size: clamp(1.6rem, 3.1vw, 2.7rem);
    line-height: 1.16;
  }
  .article-copy > h2 { margin-top: var(--cyph-space-12); }
  .article-phase-grid { display: grid; gap: var(--cyph-space-4); margin-top: var(--cyph-space-12); padding: 0 var(--cyph-layout-gutter); list-style: none; }
  .article-phase-grid li {
    padding: var(--cyph-space-6);
    border-top: var(--cyph-line-structural) solid var(--cyph-border-structural);
    opacity: 0;
    transform: translateY(var(--cyph-space-4));
    transition: opacity var(--cyph-motion-editorial) var(--cyph-ease-standard), transform var(--cyph-motion-editorial) var(--cyph-ease-standard);
  }
  .article-phase-grid li.is-visible { opacity: 1; transform: none; }
  .article-phase-grid li.active { border-top-color: var(--cyph-accent-primary); }
  .phase-motion-note { margin-top: var(--cyph-space-3); color: var(--cyph-accent-highlight); font-size: .64rem; letter-spacing: .06em; text-transform: uppercase; }
  .article-sources { padding-left: 1.25rem; }
  .article-sources li + li { margin-top: var(--cyph-space-3); }
  .article-cta { border-top: var(--cyph-line-structural) solid var(--cyph-border-structural); }

  [data-reveal] { transform: translateX(-.08em); }
  [data-reveal].is-visible {
    animation: cyph-heading-reveal 680ms var(--cyph-ease-standard) both;
  }

  @keyframes cyph-heading-reveal {
    from { opacity: .12; transform: translateY(.34em) translateX(-.08em); filter: blur(3px); }
    55% { opacity: .78; filter: blur(.5px); }
    to { opacity: 1; transform: translateY(0) translateX(-.08em); filter: blur(0); }
  }

  :global(.article-phase-grid li.is-visible .phase-anagen .ipl-beam) {
    animation: cyph-ipl-beam 3.6s var(--cyph-ease-standard) infinite;
    transform-origin: 89px 89px;
  }
  :global(.article-phase-grid li.is-visible .phase-anagen .ipl-pulse) {
    fill: none;
    stroke: var(--cyph-accent-highlight);
    stroke-width: 1.4;
    transform-origin: 89px 89px;
    animation: cyph-ipl-pulse 3.6s var(--cyph-ease-standard) infinite;
  }
  :global(.article-phase-grid li.is-visible .phase-anagen .ipl-core) {
    fill: var(--cyph-color-soft-white);
    filter: drop-shadow(0 0 7px var(--cyph-accent-primary));
    transform-origin: 89px 89px;
    animation: cyph-ipl-core 3.6s var(--cyph-ease-standard) infinite;
  }
  :global(.article-phase-grid li.is-visible .phase-catagen .hair-fill),
  :global(.article-phase-grid li.is-visible .phase-catagen .hair-bulb) {
    transform-box: fill-box;
    transform-origin: center;
    animation: cyph-catagen 4.2s var(--cyph-ease-standard) infinite;
  }
  :global(.article-phase-grid li.is-visible .phase-catagen .follicle) {
    animation: cyph-catagen-follicle 4.2s var(--cyph-ease-standard) infinite;
  }
  :global(.article-phase-grid li.is-visible .phase-telogen .hair-bulb) {
    transform-box: fill-box;
    transform-origin: center;
    animation: cyph-telogen 4.8s var(--cyph-ease-standard) infinite;
  }
  :global(.article-phase-grid li.is-visible .phase-telogen .follicle) {
    animation: cyph-telogen-rest 4.8s var(--cyph-ease-standard) infinite;
  }
  :global(.article-phase-grid li.is-visible .phase-exogen .hair-fill) {
    transform-box: fill-box;
    transform-origin: center bottom;
    animation: cyph-exogen 3.9s var(--cyph-ease-standard) infinite;
  }
  :global(.article-phase-grid li.is-visible .phase-exogen .shed-motion) {
    animation: cyph-shed-dash 4.8s linear infinite;
  }

  @keyframes cyph-ipl-beam {
    0%, 68%, 100% { opacity: 0; }
    72% { opacity: .18; }
    77% { opacity: 1; }
    82% { opacity: .28; }
  }
  @keyframes cyph-ipl-pulse {
    0%, 72%, 100% { opacity: 0; transform: scale(.72); }
    77% { opacity: 1; transform: scale(.95); }
    86% { opacity: 0; transform: scale(1.6); }
  }
  @keyframes cyph-ipl-core {
    0%, 73%, 100% { opacity: 0; transform: scale(.55); }
    77% { opacity: 1; transform: scale(1.35); }
    83% { opacity: 0; transform: scale(.8); }
  }
  @keyframes cyph-catagen {
    0%, 58%, 100% { transform: translateY(0) scale(1); opacity: 1; }
    72% { transform: translateY(-4px) scale(.96); opacity: .82; }
    86% { transform: translateY(-2px) scale(.98); opacity: .9; }
  }
  @keyframes cyph-catagen-follicle {
    0%, 58%, 100% { stroke-opacity: .7; }
    74% { stroke-opacity: .35; }
  }
  @keyframes cyph-telogen {
    0%, 100% { opacity: .62; transform: scale(.94); }
    50% { opacity: 1; transform: scale(1.08); }
  }
  @keyframes cyph-telogen-rest {
    0%, 100% { stroke-opacity: .5; }
    50% { stroke-opacity: .82; }
  }
  @keyframes cyph-exogen {
    0%, 56%, 100% { transform: translateY(0) rotate(0deg); opacity: 1; }
    72% { transform: translateY(-7px) rotate(2deg); opacity: .9; }
    84% { transform: translateY(-11px) rotate(3deg); opacity: .55; }
  }
  @keyframes cyph-shed-dash { to { stroke-dashoffset: -10; } }

  @media (min-width: 48rem) { .article-phase-grid { grid-template-columns: repeat(2, minmax(0, 1fr)); } }
  @media (min-width: 72rem) { .article-phase-grid { grid-template-columns: repeat(4, minmax(0, 1fr)); } }
  @media (max-width: 47.99rem) {
    .article-hero h1 { font-size: clamp(2.15rem, 11vw, 3.25rem); line-height: 1.1; }
    .article-page h2 { line-height: 1.2; }
  }
  @media (prefers-reduced-motion: reduce) {
    [data-reveal], .article-phase-grid li { opacity: 1; transform: none; transition: none; animation: none !important; filter: none; }
    :global(.article-phase-grid .phase-illustration *) { animation: none !important; }
    :global(.article-phase-grid .ipl-effect) { display: none; }
  }
</style>
